  "narrative": "All twelve conditional contrasts are valid and have signed estimates whose lower confidence bounds far exceed the +0.15 composite dependency-score threshold. H51 and H52 show that the negative feature_037 contrast persists in the feature_010=0 stratum (R40: +0.833, lower +0.779) and in the smaller but adequate feature_010=1 stratum (R41: +0.763, lower +0.653). H53 and H54 show the positive feature_002 contrast persists in both feature_010 strata (R42 lower +0.719; R43 lower +0.755). H55-H58 show feature_002 remains positive in feature_037 strata (lower bounds at least +0.661) and feature_037 remains negative in feature_002 strata (signed lower bounds at least +0.684). H63-H66 complete the reciprocal check: feature_010 remains positive within feature_002 and feature_037 strata (lower bounds at least +0.744). I therefore accept each claim and close these conditional investigations as supported dataset-only mean differences. Critical limitations: these analyses condition on only one binary predictor at a time, do not jointly adjust for all three, and remain observational. They do not establish causal independence or biological mechanism. The conditional contrasts are also data-adaptive follow-ups without multiplicity correction, but the interval lower bounds are so far from zero and from the +0.15 threshold that the qualitative conclusions are robust to reasonable multiplicity inflation. The implied marginal overlaps among feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 are close to independence, so they are not simple proxy markers in this supplied dataset; however, latent common structure or interactions remain possible. The registered interaction claims H59-H62 are the next most informative analyses to test meaningful effect modification. I request independent validation of H26 because feature_002 is the only large main effect still lacking independent confirmation, while its conditional persistence suggests that validation should be scientifically decisive.",
