  "narrative": "No independent validation requests remain and no due assessments were supplied, so this synthesis uses the existing discovery evidence plus already delivered validation evidence. All conclusions are dataset-specific observational associations with a composite dependency-score endpoint; no causal, mechanistic, or generalizable claim is made. The strongest supported pattern in this dataset is dominated by three binary predictors. feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001, meaning weaker composite dependency: H13/R5/R25 give signed discovery +0.829 (95% CI +0.767 to +0.891) and signed validation +0.795 (validation-adjusted interval +0.709 to +0.881). feature_002=1 is also associated with higher outcome_001: H26/R26/R52 give discovery +0.810 (95% CI +0.745 to +0.875) and validation +0.738 (+0.644 to +0.831). feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001, meaning stronger dependency: H50/R29/R38 give signed lower-outcome +0.804 (95% CI +0.742 to +0.867) and validated +0.827 (+0.731 to +0.924). These three effects are large relative to the 0.15-unit threshold and remain broadly robust across major strata and combinations. The many interaction tests among feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 were near null or subthreshold, supporting an approximately additive dominant pattern rather than robust interactions among the core predictors.\n\nfeature_063=1 is associated with lower outcome_001, but the effect is smaller and less secure than the core pattern. The overall claim H153/R144/R155 is accepted in the controller set, with signed discovery +0.239 (95% CI +0.145 to +0.332) and signed validation +0.195 (+0.062 to +0.328); validation is directionally consistent but not comfortably above threshold. The more defensible feature_063 evidence is in contexts without the dominant predictors: core-eligible feature_010=0, feature_002=0, feature_037=0 gives H154/R156/R168 signed discovery +0.252 (+0.169 to +0.335) and signed validation +0.263 (+0.135 to +0.392). Several feature_063 category-specific contrasts are supported, including feature_034 level_001 direct contrasts H247/R238 and H248/R239, and feature_052 level_003 contexts such as H215/R207 and H218/R210. However, many category tests overlap or duplicate, intervals include subthreshold values, and interaction tests are usually unresolved or rejected. Thus feature_063 should be interpreted as a moderate, context-dependent lower-outcome signal, not a core predictor equivalent to feature_010, feature_002, or feature_037.\n\nImportant negative findings include rejection of meaningful main or interaction effects for the research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015, including their interactions with research signatures and the core predictors. feature_003 was not supported as a meaningful lower-outcome predictor overall, in core-eligible refinements, or in the feature_040 tail refinements after validation. Rare binary indicators, most categorical contrasts involving feature_046, feature_052, feature_059, feature_061, feature_062, and feature_034, feature_053 contrasts, and feature_016 under core-zero conditioning were null, near-null, or below threshold. The most persistent positive borderline finding is that feature_052 level_003 may modestly modify the feature_002 effect. Active unresolved claims H239/R230 and H242/R233 show signed interactions about +0.165 and +0.162, respectively, with 95% intervals +0.020 to +0.309 and +0.008 to +0.317. These support direction but include clearly subthreshold and near-zero values; the evidence is not sufficient to accept feature_052 level_003 as a robust effect modifier. The feature_052/feature_061 duplicate category structure also warns against treating overlapping estimates as independent replication. Other unresolved feature_063 threads include H210, H211, H213, and H173; some have suggestive point estimates but intervals that include subthreshold values, small exposed cells, overlapping categories, or validation near null.\n\nThe most informative next analyses are the active unresolved tests plus the newly registered refinements. H250 should test whether feature_063 remains lower-outcome within feature_034 level_001 when feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 are all zero; this addresses whether the feature_034 level_001 contrast survives absence of the core predictors. The new core-zero-plus-feature_003=0 direct feature_063 tests assess whether the feature_063 signal is robust to feature_003 overlap. H239 and H242, plus the new feature_002-by-feature_052 interaction restricted to feature_063=0, should determine whether the borderline feature_002 modification by feature_052 level_003 is robust or merely a multiplicity-sensitive borderline finding. If H239/H242 remain uncertain or the feature_063=0 sensitivity is near null, the conclusion should remain that feature_052 level_003 is not an established modifier. If the core-zero feature_063 tests remain clear and positive, the feature_063 finding becomes more specific and less core-predictor dependent. Otherwise, the defensible feature_063 statement should remain limited: it is a moderate lower-outcome association, strongest in contexts without the dominant feature_010/feature_002/feature_037 pattern, with uncertain category breadth and no accepted interactions.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis carry-forward. Independent validation budget exhausted; no due assessments. Observational dataset-specific only. Supported core pattern: feature_010=1 higher outcome_001, feature_002=1 higher outcome_001, feature_037=1 lower outcome_001; all large, validated where available, and approximately additive. feature_063=1 moderate lower-outcome signal; strongest and better validated in core-zero/feature_010=0 contexts, but overall validation marginal and many category claims overlapping. Negative: research markers, feature_003, feature_016 core-zero, feature_053, most categorical/rare indicators, and core interactions. Unresolved active: H239/H242 borderline feature_002 by feature_052 level_003 modification; H250 core-zero feature_063 in feature_034 level_001. New registered: core-zero+feature_003=0 feature_063 overall and within feature_034 level_001; feature_002 interaction with feature_052 level_003 restricted to feature_063=0. Priorities: H250 next; H239/H242 and feature_063=0 sensitivity next; feature_003 restriction next. Do not accept feature_052 as general modifier or feature_063 category interactions without clear new evidence. No causal or generalizable claims."
